- id: P:program/tighten
  type: program
  name: tighten
  summary: Every line of a short that runs past thirty words is said again in thirty or fewer, and no other line
    moves.
  why: every line of a short that runs past thirty words is said again in thirty or fewer, and no other line moves.
  must: []
  decided: []
  takes:
  - name: s
    type: short
  gives:
  - name: t
    type: short
  lines: 9-25
  order: 2
  body: |
    program tighten
      why: every line of a short that runs past thirty words is said again in thirty or fewer, and no
           other line moves.

      takes s: short
      gives t: short

      move tightened(l: line): line
        keeps shorter against l
        give reword l to 30 words
      end

      let changes = for each l in lines of s where words l > 30
        keep replace l with tightened l
      end
      give edit s with changes
    end
  moves:
  - P:move/tighten.tightened
  steps:
  - P:step/tighten.1
  - P:step/tighten.3
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - tighten.thym#L9-L25
    confidence: 1
